tds: use ssl_ciphers (SSLCipherList) for the TLS <= 1.2 cipher list

Since PostgreSQL 18 SSLCipherSuites holds ssl_tls13_ciphers (TLS 1.3 suite names, default "")
while SSLCipherList holds ssl_ciphers. babelfishpg_tds still passed SSLCipherSuites to
SSL_CTX_set_cipher_list(), so with ssl=on the postmaster died at startup with
"could not set the cipher list (no valid ciphers available)".

--- a/contrib/babelfishpg_tds/src/backend/tds/tds-secure-openssl.c	2026-10-05 03:40:34.460656033 +0500
+++ b/contrib/babelfishpg_tds/src/backend/tds/tds-secure-openssl.c	2026-10-05 03:40:34.467805828 +0500
@@ -289,7 +289,7 @@
 		goto error;
 
 	/* set up the allowed cipher list */
-	if (SSL_CTX_set_cipher_list(context, SSLCipherSuites) != 1)
+	if (SSL_CTX_set_cipher_list(context, SSLCipherList) != 1)
 	{
 		ereport(isServerStart ? FATAL : LOG,
 				(errcode(ERRCODE_CONFIG_FILE_ERROR),
